.TH TDE\-TMATRIX 1 "November 2026" "tde-tmatrix 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-tmatrix \- Matrix chat client for the Trinity Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-tmatrix
.RB [ \-\-minimized ]
.RB [ \-\-room
.IR room\-id ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-tmatrix
(TMatrix) is a chat client for Matrix, the open and decentralised network
for secure communication. It works with any Matrix homeserver and with
people who use other Matrix applications.
.PP
It supports direct chats and rooms, invitations, the public room
directory, formatted messages (Markdown), replies, edits, reactions,
deleting messages, pictures and files, room settings and members,
notification settings per room, several accounts, and a system tray icon
with the number of unread messages and notifications.
.PP
Direct chats and private rooms are end\-to\-end encrypted. Sessions and
people are verified by comparing emoji, and message keys are backed up
with a recovery key. The Matrix protocol and the encryption are
implemented by matrix\-rust\-sdk and vodozemac.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user; starting it again shows the window of the
running instance. Closing the window keeps TMatrix running in the system
tray if the tray icon is enabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start in the system tray without showing the window. Used by the autostart
entry when "Start TMatrix in the tray when I log in" is enabled.
.TP
.BI \-\-room " room\-id"
Open the room with this ID (for example
.IR !abcdef:example.org ).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options, including the generic TDE and TQt options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Send the message (Shift+Enter starts a new line; configurable).
.TP
.B Up
In an empty message field: edit your last message.
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel a reply or edit.
.TP
.B Alt+Down
Go to the next room with unread messages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N, Ctrl+Shift+N, Ctrl+J
Start a chat, create a room, explore rooms.
.TP
.B Ctrl+U
Send a file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMATRIX_LOG
Log level of the Matrix engine on standard error (error, warn, info, debug,
trace, or a filter like
.IR matrix_sdk=debug ).
The default is warn.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tde\-tmatrixrc
Settings and the list of accounts.
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/apps/tde\-tmatrix/accounts/
The state, message and key stores of each account, encrypted with a
passphrase kept with the login, and the cache of downloaded media.
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/apps/tde\-tmatrix/sessions/
Logins, only if the TDE Wallet is not used.
.SH NOTES
TMatrix does not create accounts; register on the web page of a homeserver
first. Voice and video calls, threads and spaces are not supported.
.PP
TMatrix was written largely with the help of an AI coding assistant and
comes without any warranty. It is not affiliated with The Matrix.org
Foundation.
